      "problem": "Evaluate $g(-3)$, where $g(x)=(x+1)^{2}-(x-2)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=-3$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =(x+1)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} \\\\ g(-3) & =(-3+1)^{2}-(-3-2)^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}-(-5)^{2} \\\\  & =4-25 \\\\  & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$",
